    "result_text": "Tasks can now have a due date, and it shows on the task list. `bin/e2e` builds and runs, and the acceptance test passes: task 1's row shows `2026-03-01` under `task-due-date`. I didn't check the new field on the form by hand; the test only seeds a task and reads the date back.\n\nThe server here is Spring Boot, not OfficeFloor as the request says. The only OfficeFloor reference is the package name, `net.officefloor.hq.app`, so I followed the Spring setup that's actually in the code.\n\n- **Database:** a new migration, `V47__task_due_date.sql`, adds an optional `due_date` column to the `task` table. Existing tasks simply have no date.\n- **Server:** a task now stores an optional due date. You can set it when adding a task, and the task list returns it as `YYYY-MM-DD`. The test seed endpoint also accepts `dueDate` for tasks.\n- **Front end:**\n  - The add-task form has an optional \"Due date\" date picker (`data-testid=\"task-form-due-date\"`).\n  - The task table has a new \"Due date\" column (`data-testid=\"task-due-date\"` in each row), which is blank when a task has no date.\n  - All existing `data-testid` values are unchanged.\n\nThe front-end changes are in `project-tasks.ts` and `task.service.ts`.",
